# Baseline: every text file is LF in the working tree, including on a Windows
# checkout. Without this, a Windows editor rewrites prose, YAML and .tf files to
# CRLF and the whole tree shows as modified with an empty whitespace-only diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The rules below are redundant under the baseline, but they record *why* LF is
# load-bearing for these paths; keep them if the baseline is ever narrowed.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Python scripts run directly by their shebang; a CRLF shebang fails with 'python3\r: No such file'
*.py text eol=lf
# Files that run on the firewall or are loaded by it must be LF even on a Windows checkout (a CRLF shebang exits 127)
scripts/firewall/* text eol=lf
network/*.xml text eol=lf
# Role files are copied to Linux guests and may be executed (exercise1 has no extension); keep LF on a Windows checkout
ansible/roles/*/files/* text eol=lf
